      {
        /* **The terms exist now, and this is the link the placeholder was holding open.** It
        used to say they were "still to be confirmed by the committee, and will be linked here
        before entries open" — a sentence that goes false the moment the page exists, on the
        one control whose whole job is to be a truthful statement of what somebody is agreeing
        to.

        **It claims no committee involvement, because there is none.** The race director
        supplied the copy on 28 August 2026 and the committee has not ratified it; the version
        line at the foot of `/nn/2026/terms/` says exactly that, and this sentence says nothing
        about provenance at all rather than repeating a claim that would have to be kept in
        step with it.

        **The checkbox and its label are untouched**, and `id="entry-terms-hint"` is unchanged
        so `aria-describedby` on the input still resolves — the hint is read out after the
        label, which is what puts the link in front of somebody using a screen reader before
        they tick rather than after.

        **The year is derived, not written.** `${Astro.url.pathname}terms/` is the same idiom
        the form's own `action` uses a few lines down, and for the same reason: this component
        is rendered from `/nn/<year>/`, and a literal `/nn/2026/terms/` here would be a second
